# 11. The best tag system

Use this hierarchy:

```txt
Global concepts:
Broad essay topic.

Local concepts:
What this specific frame is about.

Frame label:
Unique poetic name.

Rhetorical role:
Standardized analytics category.

Visual motifs:
What appears visually.

Asset concepts:
Glossary-linked concepts attached to the actual chosen image/clip.
```

Example:

```json
{
  "frame_label": "Earth Turned Inside Out",
  "rhetorical_role": "expansion",
  "global_concepts": ["ecology", "Gaia", "nonhuman agency"],
  "local_concepts": ["Gaia", "earthbound", "enclosure"],
  "visual_motifs": ["sphere", "atmosphere", "cosmological diagram"],
  "asset_concepts": ["anima mundi", "world soul", "macrocosm"]
}
```

Why this works:

```txt
global_concepts tells you the essay category
local_concepts tells you the moment
frame_label lets humans understand it
rhetorical_role lets analytics compare structure
visual_motifs lets you learn what images work
asset_concepts ties it to the glossary
```

That is the best balance.

